Gears of War 3 DLSS calibration: gow2_depth_reversed (default true, the Gears of War 2 behaviour)
says whether the scene depth holds 1 - z; it drives the motion vector shader and the DLSS/FSR
depth-inverted flags. Gears of War 3 stores plain z. The vertical FOV and near plane are read
from the ViewProjection columns, so a matrix that includes the view rotation (Gears of War 3's
camera-relative ViewProjection) gives the right values.

--- a/src/graphics/d3d12/gow2_temporal.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/d3d12/gow2_temporal.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@
